---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Guilloche from '../components/Guilloche.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About — Signatif"
  description="Signatif is the Sealed Interoperable Graduated Non-repudiable Anchored Trust Infrastructure Framework, a CalConnect standard for verifiable artifacts in regulated industries."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="A standard for verifiable artifacts, developed in CalConnect"
    lede="Signatif — the Sealed Interoperable Graduated Non-repudiable Anchored Trust Infrastructure Framework — is developed in CalConnect, The Calendaring and Scheduling Consortium."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-14">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr]">
      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
        <p>
          Signatif specifies a trust infrastructure for artifacts whose
          trustworthiness carries legal, economic, or safety consequences:
          conformity certificates, calibration records, test results, and
          compliance attestations issued in regulated industries.
        </p>
        <p>
          The framework binds signing authority to a multi-dimensional
          authorization scope, establishes artifact trustworthiness through
          the convergence of independent attestations from multiple trust
          dimensions, and treats trust as a lifecycle — granted, sustained,
          and withdrawn through formal threshold-gated mechanisms.
        </p>
        <p>
          The standard defines requirements, not products. Fourteen
          requirements classes — from architecture and artifact format
          through verification, transparency, revocation, and algorithm
          agility — each carry a matching conformance class, so
          "conforming implementation" is a testable claim. Registries are
          maintained by implementing schemes, which keeps national and
          regulatory algorithm choices where they belong.
        </p>
        <div class="border-l-2 border-seal-600 pl-5">
          <p class="expanded text-lg font-semibold text-ink">The name</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-ink-2">
            From Latin <span class="italic">signare</span> — to mark with a
            seal, to sign; the root of <em>sign</em>, <em>signature</em>,
            and <em>signet</em>. The premise is in the stem:
            trustworthiness is established by what is verifiably signed,
            not by who is trusted.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-6">
        <div class="shadow-panel relative overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-rule bg-panel p-6">
          <Guilloche class="absolute -bottom-16 -right-16 size-52 text-azure-600/20" rings={20} seed={5} />
          <p class="label-mono relative text-ink-3">At a glance</p>
          <dl class="relative mt-4 divide-y divide-rule-faint">
            {[
              ['Name', 'Signatif'],
              ['Expands to', 'Sealed Interoperable Graduated Non-repudiable Anchored Trust Infrastructure Framework'],
              ['Developed in', 'CalConnect'],
              ['Form', 'Requirements + conformance classes'],
              ['License', 'Standard source on GitHub'],
            ].map(([k, v]) => (
              <div class="grid gap-1 py-3 sm:grid-cols-[7.5rem_1fr] sm:gap-3">
                <dt class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-3">{k}</dt>
                <dd class="text-sm font-medium text-ink">{v}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-rule-faint bg-panel p-6">
          <p class="label-mono text-ink-3">Get involved</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-2">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/CalConnect/cc-signatif" class="font-medium text-azure-700 transition-colors hover:text-ink">Read and clone the standard</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/CalConnect/cc-signatif/issues" class="font-medium text-azure-700 transition-colors hover:text-ink">Open an issue</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://www.calconnect.org/" class="font-medium text-azure-700 transition-colors hover:text-ink">Participate via CalConnect</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
